      "severity": "CONCERN",
      "title": "StrEnum values can bypass runtime type validation",
      "description": "`TimeMeaning` is a `StrEnum`, so a plain string such as `\"period_start\"` compares equal to `TimeMeaning.PERIOD_START` and passes the membership check. The `Market` then stores a plain string despite the field\u2019s enum contract. The same equality issue lets `calendar_id_for(\"extended\")` and `require_adjustment_basis(\"raw\")` accept plain strings. Additionally, `_normalize_bases` converts its input to a `frozenset` before checking element types; `[AdjustmentBasis.RAW, \"raw\"]` can therefore deduplicate to the enum and be accepted, silently discarding an invalid element. Validate enum types before membership checks and before normalization.",
